DIAGNOSIS
---------
OpenLane 2 uses Linux process-management signals internally (SIGKILL in
openlane/steps/magic.py). Windows does not expose SIGKILL in the Python
signal module; the equivalent SIGTERM exists but SIGKILL does not. This
is a known platform limitation — OpenLane 2 is not supported on native
Windows; it requires Linux (bare-metal or WSL2/Docker).

